{"title":"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d745b81add053aa31f45d72cb9a898e3441e74bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, a_3, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" /> be an infinite sequence of positive integers, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be a positive integer. Suppose that, for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a54df70ab4e8f05a9ad4b78a1dad57715beaca39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is equal to the number of times <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/896d56965b17443a55b2b5e55f798adf6465380d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" /> appears in the list <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/c/bdc0e230e464d7e2fdb46c853605b14f90cdae0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Prove that at least one of the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a12579f641ac40efcd17df27ce7ca127b259348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_3, a_5, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da50250ea87137598672fc1cfc83315e53214ebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2, a_4, a_6, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"13\" /> is eventually periodic.\n</p><p>(An infinite sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/01167aa6970401049efeb971b45b937eded09bfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1, b_2, b_3, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" /> is eventually periodic if there exist positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d258f622b3df20c526f886c1ef62fb6baa4b623b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{m+p} = b_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"84\" height=\"19\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c84cf8abb7a13a2f1d05b3ebe0ea63efc6f672f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\ge M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ASV1dZCuWGs\">https://youtu.be/ASV1dZCuWGs</a> (in full detail!)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO\" title=\"2024 IMO\">2024 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20